    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d862">

                <pb facs="0929" n="1763" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1763"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/9158</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schmedeman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Christiania</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-12T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 12, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 13, 12.50
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>581. The following official announcement appeared in the press this morning:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The German Minister in Christiania has informed the Foreign Office that
                            owing to previous British declarations that the North Sea is a war
                                zone<anchor n="1" xml:id="d862-f1"/> and the German Bay (Heligoland
                            [Bight]) a danger zone,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d862-f2"/> the Imperial
                            German Government is obliged, in order to meet the situation created by
                            the said declarations, to proceed to the extraordinary measure of
                            warning neutral ships against navigating in the German Bay and against
                            further dangers to which it becomes necessary to expose neutral ships in
                            consequence of British warfare in this zone. The danger of navigating in
                            this zone can only be avoided by following special directions which can
                            be obtained from the German naval authorities.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schmedeman</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
